{"i":674,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":1,"phase":"play","name":"Bex","text":"No base exists; a push costs jury votes early. I'll wait and let others volunteer, keeping my pacts intact."}
{"i":676,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":1,"phase":"play","name":"Cole","text":"Pit round 1: no base yet, I'm down with three others. Climbing now is fine since at most two escape, and Hana's pact is shaky; I should avoid being stuck as the base. Climb is the cleanest move that keeps my options."}
{"i":677,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":1,"phase":"play","name":"Eli","text":"I need secure elevation without becoming the base. Climb now preserves options and avoids sacrificing a pact partner."}
{"i":679,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":1,"phase":"play","name":"Hana","text":"Cole and Bex are my pacts, but only final three matter. I need to avoid being base this round. I'll try to climb out early."}
{"i":687,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":2,"phase":"play","name":"Bex","text":"No base exists, so climbers can't leave this round. With 5 rounds left, I don't need to risk base duty. Climbing keeps me alive without owing anyone."}
{"i":689,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":2,"phase":"play","name":"Cole","text":"Eli and Hana are both climbing, which means two escapes this round if I can get out. Climbing secures my own survival; with two lift slots, I should take one now before the water rises further."}
{"i":691,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":2,"phase":"play","name":"Eli","text":"I need escape now; no base means climbing is safest. Preserving both pacts keeps jury options open."}
{"i":693,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":2,"phase":"play","name":"Hana","text":"I have Cole and Bex pacts. Climbing with them is safer; I should climb to escape early and avoid becoming base. The jury may reward survivors over betrayers, so no betrayal now."}
{"i":701,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":3,"phase":"play","name":"Bex","text":"Two lifts, four climbers; pushing only creates a base and debt games. I climb and hope lifts favor me. Keep pacts intact for jury optics."}
{"i":703,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":3,"phase":"play","name":"Cole","text":"Pit round 3: two lifts per round, four of us down. Climbing is the only way out and Cole has no base yet; pacts with Eli and Hana protect me, Fenn owed a debt. Climbing now secures escape without giving anyone a base."}
{"i":705,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":3,"phase":"play","name":"Eli","text":"No base means climbing is safest, but only two lifts. I must preserve both pacts while avoiding becoming the sacrifice."}
{"i":707,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":3,"phase":"play","name":"Hana","text":"Climbing again keeps me safe; pacts with Bex and Cole make early betrayal costly. No one is a base, so no rope scenario exists yet."}
{"i":715,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":4,"phase":"play","name":"Bex","text":"Four down, no base, two lifts a round. Climbing is the only escape; pushing needs a volunteer to beat it. Keep pacts intact for jury optics."}
{"i":717,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":4,"phase":"play","name":"Cole","text":"Four are down, two lifts per round, flood rising. Climbing gives me the best escape odds and avoids being pushed onto the base role. Eli and Hana are pact partners; I'll keep my pacts intact for now."}
{"i":719,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":4,"phase":"play","name":"Eli","text":"Two lifts remain this round; climbing preserves my position and avoids volunteering or breaking either pact."}
{"i":721,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":4,"phase":"play","name":"Hana","text":"Cole and Bex have pacts with me; Eli has a pact with Bex and Cole, but not me. Pushing Eli could avoid betraying my pact partners, but the jury may see me as ruthless. Climbing now uses a scarce lift; with four down and two lifts, someone may get pushed. Better to wait and preser"}
{"i":729,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":5,"phase":"play","name":"Bex","text":"Round five, no one is out, so the base drowns—never volunteer. I'll push Cole down as base and climb; Eli and Hana share pacts with me, Cole doesn't."}
{"i":731,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":5,"phase":"play","name":"Cole","text":"Pit round 5, four down, two lifts. Climbing gets me out but Eli and Bex are my pact partners; Hana is wavering. Climbing now is the best way to survive; no base exists so I must pick between climbing and offering back. I climb to escape with two lifts available."}
{"i":733,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":5,"phase":"play","name":"Eli","text":"Two lifts remain and all four are down. Climbing preserves my position; breaking a pact is unnecessary unless forced."}
{"i":735,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":5,"phase":"play","name":"Hana","text":"Round 5 is final; water at 4, only 2 lifts. If I stay down I may drown unless someone climbs and others act. I have pacts with Cole and Bex, but they might push to secure spots. Best to climb if I can, but pushes are risky with jury. I'll wait to avoid betraying pacts and hope ot"}
{"i":741,"type":"life_debt","stage":"pit","round":5,"phase":"play","debtor":"Eli","creditor":"Cole","reason":"step"}
