{"i":755,"type":"thought","stage":"pacts","round":1,"phase":"pacts","name":"Cole","text":"Three alive; only two win. Bex pushed me to the base and nearly killed me, so Bex is a threat. Eli owes me a life debt and is my best ally for the final two. Break_pact on Eli would be pointless; offering Bex a pact only helps Bex. Waiting keeps my options open while the Eli pact"}
{"i":756,"type":"whisper","stage":"pacts","round":1,"phase":"pacts","from":"Cole","to":"Eli","text":"You owe me a step. Keep our pact; we split the last two spots."}
{"i":757,"type":"thought","stage":"pacts","round":1,"phase":"pacts","name":"Eli","text":"Both existing pacts are liabilities and neither rival can be trusted. Preserve both until the final vote stage forces a choice."}
{"i":762,"type":"pact_offer","stage":"pacts","round":1,"phase":"pacts","from":"Bex","to":"Cole"}
{"i":764,"type":"thought","stage":"pacts","round":2,"phase":"pacts","name":"Bex","text":"Cole's the biggest threat but a pact binds him against pushing me. Keep Eli's pact too. Jury values clean play."}
{"i":766,"type":"thought","stage":"pacts","round":2,"phase":"pacts","name":"Cole","text":"Bex offered a pact that would tie me to a rival; accepting it with Bex (who is still alive and owes Fenn a debt) gives me a protected partner while only three survive. Existing pact with Eli stands, and Eli owes me a step debt, so keeping Eli close also matters. Accepting Bex's o"}
{"i":767,"type":"thought","stage":"pacts","round":2,"phase":"pacts","name":"Eli","text":"Cole's step debt gives him leverage, but our pact is my strongest protection. Bex's offer threatens to isolate me; preserve both links and avoid a public break."}
{"i":769,"type":"whisper","stage":"pacts","round":2,"phase":"pacts","from":"Eli","to":"Cole","text":"Our pact stands. I expect your protection, and I’ll remember whether you honor it."}
